      "writtenOn": "2025-10-25T21:51:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e nit: might be useful to clarify that it will be a per-vCPU memcache, not per VM (which is why we cannot just remember this pointer in struct pkvm_pgtable, and need to pass it around instead)?\n\nSure, I will mention per-vCPU memcache (I\u0027ve mentioned it later in this patch-set but this is first one related to this memcache so it is better to mention it here).\n\n\u003e BTW I imagine we could avoid passing it around: since we eventually feed the pages from the memcache to the per-VM pool (in guest_mmu_put_page()) anyway\n\nThey are put to the per-VM pool quite rarely: note that guest_mmu_put_page actually call __hyp_put_page which puts the page to the pool only when the page is not used anymore (hyp_page_ref_dec_and_test(p)), which happen mostly during VM teardown (could happen due to MMU notifiers, e.g. when ballooning jumps in but even then it is rare that all PTE for a given page-table page (all 512 PTE) are not used and therefore page table page is freed and put to the pool). I\u0027ve also propose improved commit log here: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/3702537/comment/afd7c32e_22600f0b/\n\n\u003e I guess the only reason not to do that is the unneeded overhead of attaching the page to the pool in hyp_put_page() -\u003e __hyp_attach_page() every time.\n\nYeah seems like unneeded overhead.",
      "parentUuid": "0341e653_947e0dfb",
      "revId": "d8cd595401ec40e98bfb84c648b7fa45d7ab59be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6b7b4e_ad2e7018",
